TRACE_CALL 24 name=apply_patch args="*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /work/verification.k\n@@\n   syntax Int ::= oddDigitProduct(Int, Int) [function]\n+               | oddDigitStep(Bool, Int, Int, Int) [function]\n \n   rule oddDigitProduct(0, A:Int) => A\n \n   rule oddDigitProduct(N:Int, A:Int)\n-    => oddDigitProduct(\n-         (N -Int pyMod(N, 10)) /Int 10,\n-         A)\n-    requires N >Int 0\n-     andBool pyMod(N, 2) =/=Int 1\n-\n-  rule oddDigitProduct(N:Int, 0)\n-    => oddDigitProduct(\n-         (N -Int pyMod(N, 10)) /Int 10,\n-         pyMod(N, 10))\n-    requires N >Int 0\n-     andBool pyMod(N, 2) ==Int 1\n-\n-  rule oddDigitProduct(N:Int, A:Int)\n-    => oddDigitProduct(\n-         (N -Int pyMod(N, 10)) /Int 10,\n-         A *Int pyMod(N, 10))\n-    requires N >Int 0\n-     andBool A =/=Int 0\n-     andBool pyMod(N, 2) ==Int 1\n+    => oddDigitStep(\n+         pyMod(N, 2) ==Int 1,\n+         (N -Int pyMod(N, 10)) /Int 10,\n+         pyMod(N, 10),\n+         A)\n+    requires N >Int 0\n+\n+  rule oddDigitStep(false, Q:Int, _:Int, A:Int)\n+    => oddDigitProduct(Q, A)\n+\n+  rule oddDigitStep(true, Q:Int, D:Int, 0)\n+    => oddDigitProduct(Q, D)\n+\n+  rule oddDigitStep(true, Q:Int, D:Int, A:Int)\n+    => oddDigitProduct(Q, A *Int D)\n+    requires A =/=Int 0\n endmodule\n*** End Patch\n"
